Z||000000||Robert||09-10-2000||02:32 PM||||Hi all; just got home from the show and though you guys/gals would enjoy some the photo’s.  I was surprised by all the Fiero conversions at this show.  I was at last year’s show and there were only two Fiero’s.  Don’t ask me what the Batman type car is all I know is it started out as a Jag XKE<BR> <A HREF="http://community.webshots.com/album/4721870MnPgiqHXuI" TARGET=_blank>http://community.webshots.com/album/4721870MnPgiqHXuI</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||pherder||09-10-2000||03:07 PM||||Great shots!  <P>You might want to re-label the F50s (first couple of pictures labeled F40s).<P>The red F40 was correct.<P>I have seen that 308 before and I STILL don't like a Fiero wing on it!!<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||09-10-2000||03:37 PM||||pherder;<BR>Thanks for the F-50 information.  I can’t tell one from the other, except the F-50 was a much nicer looking car and the finish was cleaner. I went to this year’s show because there was supposed to be a Diablo there, but it was a no-show on Saturday. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fsrowsell||09-10-2000||08:00 PM||||Robert,do you know who produces the F50 kit. I wouldn't mind building one of those for myself....<BR>||||reg||1
