Z||000007||mshill||09-10-2000||09:50 PM||||The F50 looks like it was a non-stretch version, but I cannot tell from the pictures.  The convertible top was definitely a custion thing that does not seem to be part of the kit.  I would bet that body came from the link above.  I wish I wasn't so busy yesterday or I would have gone out to the show to see them.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Babygirl||09-11-2000||02:00 AM||||We were at that show!  I was suprised that there were soooooooo many Cobras!  And only a few Fiero conversions!  Did you see that black 1988 SE Fiero with the Cadillac Northstar engine?  Wow!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>~Laura||||reg||1
Z||000009||Robert||09-11-2000||02:44 PM||||Sorry I missed you Lauara, I was there on Saturday.  If you were there on Sunday, was there a Diablo showing?  He was a no show on Saturday.   I loved that Northstar SE, the dash wasn’t bad either.  If you haven’t already checked out the pictures I took of the SE, take a look at the link above.<BR>As for the Cobras, there is always a BIG turnout of those.  I am a member of the Kit Car Club, so I see them all the time.  I even went on a “Snake Run” with them one time.  Those cars are incredibly fast, and handled great on a “spirited” run through the Napa Valley.  My poor 87GT could not keep up with them, and my breaks were smoking by then end of the trip. <BR>||||reg||10
